From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Sanchez <nathanasanchez@google.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:51:27 -0500
Subject: [pending][8078 after build 47] [M156] [Ganesh] Restrict scissor by
 dst-read bounds

FlyWeb: Skia 9d96dfeb45 from the branch-heads/8078 roll 7cd7567 (7dc6c0c3424a..9d96dfeb451c),
applied on the pending Skia tree 47b14cb49e (after skia/0002). Same patch-id as upstream (a80446c2f5).

Original change's description:
> [Ganesh] Restrict scissor by dst-read bounds
>
> This ensures that we always intersect the scissor send to the pipeline
> with any dst-read bounds, and always perform a scissor if we have a
> dst-read. While geometry that may overshoot the draw bounds due to an
> incorrect bounds calculation may still be rasterized when rendering
> without a dst-read, anytime there is one those pixels would be clipped
> out scissor.
>
